// Package registry: `use <name>` of a name found in no local search directory loads packages/<name>/<name>.warp, the
// package fetched once; a package without that module only brings files. Most packages need no line here: the default
// registry github.com/pannous/warp-packages holds one folder per package (`use colors` is its colors/, latest), and a
// folder whose manifest package.warp names a `repository` is a proxy for that repository (`use uniscript`).
// A line here pins or redirects a package:
//   name: 1.2.3                 the default registry's package at its tag name@1.2.3 (latest: its default branch)
//   name: "owner/repo@1.2.3"    a GitHub repository at its tag v1.2.3; unquoted owner/repo follows its default branch
//   name: "git url"             any repository ("github:owner/repo" too), following its default branch
//   name: {repository: owner/repo, version: 1.2.3, library: "c/ffi/x"}   the long form, which a manifest also uses
// A pinned version is cloned once per machine into ~/.cache/warp/packages/<name>@1.2.3 (a tag never changes) and linked
// as packages/<name>. Raise the version to update. A local checkout stands in for a fetch: ln -s ~/dev/uniscript packages/uniscript
